      "content": "Originalism is a specific judicial philosophy, not the universally accepted standard in constitutional law today, though it is highly influential in certain legal circles. It is in direct contrast to \"living constitutionalism,\" which argues that the Constitution must be interpreted in light of evolving societal values and modern needs. While originalism prioritizes fixed historical meaning, living constitutionalism favors a more dynamic and adaptable view of the text to address contemporary life.",
